ARM: add rp2350_defconfig for the FRANK Core 2 Proto slave half

Derived from mps2_defconfig, which is the closest existing v7-M NOMMU target,
with four substantive changes:

  DRAM_BASE/SIZE   0x11000000 / 8 MB -- the QMI chip-select 1 window, which is
                   where the external PSRAM appears. The internal SRAM is
                   deliberately not system RAM: it belongs to core 1.

  BINFMT_ELF_FDPIC replaces BINFMT_FLAT. bFLT needs one contiguous allocation
                   per process covering text and data together, and 8 MB cannot
                   supply it once the kernel and initramfs are resident -- a
                   bFLT userspace on this board reached a shell that could not
                   start a single external command.

  FRANK_RING_CONSOLE replaces the MPS2 UART. This half has no wired UART and the
                   RP2350's USB controller has no Linux driver, so core 1 serves
                   the console through an SRAM ring.

  ARM_MPU is on. The M33 reports PMSAv8, unified, with 8 regions.

Networking is dropped wholesale: there is no interface on this half and the
stack is pure overhead in 8 MB.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/rp2350_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+CONFIG_NO_HZ_IDLE=y
+CONFIG_HIGH_RES_TIMERS=y
+CONFIG_PREEMPT_VOLUNTARY=y
+CONFIG_LOG_BUF_SHIFT=16
+CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE=y
+CONFIG_EXPERT=y
+# CONFIG_UID16 is not set
+CONFIG_BASE_SMALL=y
+# CONFIG_FUTEX is not set
+# CONFIG_EPOLL is not set
+# CONFIG_SIGNALFD is not set
+# CONFIG_EVENTFD is not set
+# CONFIG_AIO is not set
+# CONFIG_MMU is not set
+CONFIG_ARCH_RP2350=y
+CONFIG_SET_MEM_PARAM=y
+CONFIG_DRAM_BASE=0x11000000
+CONFIG_DRAM_SIZE=0x800000
+# CONFIG_ATAGS is not set
+# CONFIG_SUSPEND is not set
+# CONFIG_BLOCK is not set
+CONFIG_BINFMT_ELF_FDPIC=y
+# CONFIG_COREDUMP is not set
+# CONFIG_VM_EVENT_COUNTERS is not set
+CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
+CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
+# CONFIG_FW_LOADER is not set
+# CONFIG_INPUT is not set
+# CONFIG_SERIO is not set
+# CONFIG_VT is not set
+# CONFIG_LEGACY_PTYS is not set
+# CONFIG_HW_RANDOM is not set
+# CONFIG_HWMON is not set
+CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
+CONFIG_ARM_SP805_WATCHDOG=y
+CONFIG_MFD_SYSCON=y
+# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
+CONFIG_NEW_LEDS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_CLASS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_SYSCON=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGERS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_TIMER=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_ONESHOT=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_HEARTBEAT=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_BACKLIGHT=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_CPU=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_DEFAULT_ON=y
+CONFIG_ARM_TIMER_SP804=y
+# CONFIG_DNOTIFY is not set
+# CONFIG_INOTIFY_USER is not set
+# CONFIG_MISC_FILESYSTEMS is not set
+CONFIG_NFS_FS=y
+CONFIG_NFS_V4=y
+CONFIG_NFS_V4_1=y
+CONFIG_NFS_V4_2=y
+CONFIG_ROOT_NFS=y
+CONFIG_NLS=y
+CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME=y
+# CONFIG_ENABLE_MUST_CHECK is not set
+# CONFIG_DEBUG_BUGVERBOSE is not set
+CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_DWARF_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULT=y
+CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
+# CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG is not set
+# CONFIG_SCHED_DEBUG is not set
+CONFIG_MEMTEST=y
+
+#
+# FRANK Core 2 Proto, slave half.
+#
+# Networking is dropped wholesale: there is no interface on this half, and in
+# 8 MB of RAM the stack is pure overhead.
+#
+
+# Uniprocessor is load-bearing, not a simplification. ARM_NO_EXCLUSIVES replaces
+# LDREX/STREX with interrupt masking, which is atomic only against this core.
+# CONFIG_SMP is not set
+
+# Console served by core 1 through an SRAM ring; there is no usable UART on this
+# half and the RP2350's USB controller has no Linux driver.
+CONFIG_FRANK_RING_CONSOLE=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_CORE=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_CORE_CONSOLE=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_EARLYCON=y
+
+# TIMER0 as clocksource and clockevent; ARMV7M_SYSTICK gives only the former.
+CONFIG_CLKSRC_RP2350=y
+
+# The MPU is off for first boot.
+#
+# The hardware has a real one -- PMSAv8, unified, 8 regions (hw-findings F6) --
+# but the kernel's region layout covers system RAM, and this board's console
+# lives in SRAM at 0x2007e000, outside it. Bring the board up first and turn the
+# MPU on as a separate, testable step.
+# CONFIG_ARM_MPU is not set
+
+CONFIG_OF=y
+CONFIG_USE_OF=y
